# Everything a trial run produces is ephemeral. Only the harness, the prompts and
# the written-up findings belong in the repository.
#
# These rules live here rather than in .git/info/exclude so they reach whoever
# runs a trial next. A local exclude would have protected only the machine that
# happened to create it, and the first thing a run generates is a 200KB
# transcript sitting next to tracked files.

# Full request/response log of a run. Large, regenerated every time, and a run's
# findings are written up rather than read from it.
transcript.md
*.log

# Crates an agent wrote during a trial. They are evidence of what the docs led it
# to build, not code this repository ships, and they trip the workspace
# Cargo.toml conventions because they are not workspace members.
nym-chat-demo/
nym-chat-app/
nym-*-demo/
nym-*-app/

# A credential, if anyone puts one here rather than at the repository root.
.bypass
